 | `dfo.on(event, fn)` | listen; answers a function that stops listening. An event the manifest does not list is **refused** with a warning, not delivered |
 | `dfo.store.get(key, fallback)`, `.set(key, value)` | the module's own settings, apart from every other module's (`dfjs-module-<id>` in the game's own storage) |
 | `dfo.say(text)` | a line over the game |
-| `dfo.onKey('F7', fn)` / `'Shift+F7'` | a key, never from a text field |
+| `dfo.onKey('F7', fn)` / `'Shift+F7'` | a key, never from a text field and never with Ctrl, Alt or Meta held |
+| `dfo.retarget([x, z])` / `dfo.retarget(null)` | ask the game to mark that place on its compass instead of the tracked quest's - the HUD's own compass, and every module that follows `questMark`, see it (the last ask by an enabled module wins; a module switched off asks no more); `null` gives the compass back |
 
 The handle is frozen and has no door to the net, the disk or another module. A listener that throws is isolated - the frame
 and every other module go on - and a module that fails 25 times is switched off for the session.
@@ -116,12 +117,20 @@ entry's `sha256`.
 
 | module | listens to | does |
 | --- | --- | --- |
-| `waypoint` | `questMark` | a gold diamond in the view over the compass's quest mark, with the distance, an edge arrow when it is to a side (F7) |
+| `waypoint` | `questMark`, `drawFx` | a diamond over the compass's mark at its own spot on the floor, in perspective, with the distance and - walking - the time at the player's pace; dim behind a wall; an edge arrow when it is off to a side (F7; Shift+F3 cycles its look: gold, ivory, cyan, magenta, large) |
 | `quest-tracker` | `quests`, `questMark` | a panel listing every active quest: where, time left, the latest entry (Shift+F7) |
 | `guide-trail` | `questMark`, `drawFx` | gold embers along the way to the quest, or back the way the player came (F4): the embers are a pure function of a path and the clock; pools lie on the floor as translucent stains and sparks rise additively, so the trail reads on snow as well as in a dungeon |
 
+| `pins` | `questMark`, `drawFx` | F2 drops a pin where the crosshair meets the world, F3 cycles the compass quest -> pins -> quest, Shift+F2 removes the followed pin; arriving removes it; a jump of 150 m (a new place, its own frame) clears them. It asks the game to mark the pin (`retarget`), so the compass, waypoint and trail follow it with no module reading another |
+
+The guide trail plans round walls over the floor from the world probe (`route.js`); where the mark is shut in a building and the host hands over `world.doors` it leads to the door nearest the mark (the street host does; the loader's released-client route has no door list and leads to the nearest cell). Shift+F4 cycles its look.
+
 Each is one folder and lives with or without the others; none reads another.
 
+### KEYS - and the game's own
+
+The game binds F5 (character sheet), F6 (inventory), F8 (screenshot), F9/F11 (quick save/load), F10 (HUD) and the letters, digits and arrows in play; in dialogs and the maps it binds F1-F8 again. The modules use F2, F3, F4, F7 (and Shift with F2, F3, F4, F7) - none a gameplay default - and each key does nothing unless the HUD has drawn in the last 400 ms, so a dialog, a menu or a map that uses the same F key is never also answered by a module. `test/mods1_api.test.js` reads the game's default bindings and fails if a module takes one, if two modules share a key, or if a key is not gated.
+
 ## KNOWN LIMITS
 
 - `drawFx` and `questMark` are announced by the world-hosted scenes (the street, a building, a dungeon entered from the world).
